# {% if is_codex %}@hm-personalization-audit{% else %}/hm:personalization-audit{% endif %}

> Composite-score personalization audit (ADR-011). Reads
> `.claude/observability/adaptive/overrides.jsonl` (Phase 9 telemetry) +
> harness.yaml + detection cache, computes the three-layer score, ranks
> ActionItems by ADR-011 evidence schema. **100% local — no network.**

## Layers

| Layer | Weight | What it measures |
|-------|------:|------------------|
| `l1_conversion` | 0.4 | (medium_accepted + high_silent) / total_recommendations |
| `l2_stability`  | 0.3 | 100 − min(100, override_events_last_30d × 5) |
| `l3_cadence`    | 0.3 | adaptive opt-in + audit cadence regularity |

Tiers: bronze (0-39) · silver (40-64) · gold (65-84) · platinum (85-100).

## Run

```bash
!uv run --with {{ harness_maker_src_path }} python -m harness_maker.personalization_audit .
```

The command:
1. Loads the locked rubric from the harness-maker package.
2. Reads overrides.jsonl (schema_version-filtered).
3. Reads `.claude/harness.yaml` for AdaptiveConfig + high-confidence comments.
4. Reads the detection cache for `total_recommendations`.
5. Stamps `.claude/observability/adaptive/last-audit.txt` with the current
   ISO timestamp (atomic write) — this feeds L3 on the next run.
6. Prints composite score, per-layer scores, ranked ActionItems with
   `{n_observations, top_3_signals, confidence}` evidence per item.

## Interpreting results

- **Bronze (< 40)** — likely a fresh install or telemetry opted out. L3
  often dominates. Either accept (privacy-by-design) or enable telemetry.
- **Silver (40-64)** — conversion working but stability low. Look at the
  top axis_path in the ActionItems — repeated overrides usually indicate
  the default is wrong for this project.
- **Gold (65-84)** — strong personalization. ActionItems are tuning hints.
- **Platinum (≥ 85)** — defaults match user intent, cadence is regular.

## Acting on ActionItems

{% if is_codex %}For Codex: read the printed list; each item carries
priority + suggestion + evidence. Use `request_user_input` to confirm
before applying any default change to harness.yaml.{% else %}For each
ActionItem with priority `P0` or `P1`, use `AskQuestion` (Cursor) or
`AskUserQuestion` (Claude Code) to ask the user whether to apply the
suggested default change. The audit itself is read-only — it never
edits harness.yaml.{% endif %}

The `evidence.confidence` bucket follows ADR-004/007:
- `HIGH` (≥ 5 observations) — strong signal, change the default.
- `MEDIUM` (2-4) — suggestive, ask the user.
- `LOW` (1) — noise, surface but do not propose action.

## Autoloop behavior

Read-only. Safe to run inside an iteration verify step; the only side
effect is the last-audit.txt timestamp update (idempotent across runs).

